  "content": {
    "id": "p47-q12-answer",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "If $x^4-2x^3-20x^2+mx+n$ is exactly divisible by $x^2-5x+2$, find $m$ and $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=41$, $n=-14$. Long division gives remainder $(m-41)x+(n+14)$; exact divisibility requires both coefficients to be zero.",
      "worked": "The successive quotient terms in long division are $x^2$, $3x$ and $-7$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(x^4-2x^3-20x^2+mx+n)-x^2(x^2-5x+2)&=3x^3-22x^2+mx+n\\\\\n(3x^3-22x^2+mx+n)-3x(x^2-5x+2)&=-7x^2+(m-6)x+n\\\\\n(-7x^2+(m-6)x+n)-(-7)(x^2-5x+2)&=(m-41)x+(n+14).\n\\end{aligned}$$\nThus\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nx^4-2x^3-20x^2+mx+n&=(x^2-5x+2)(x^2+3x-7)+(m-41)x+(n+14).\n\\end{aligned}$$\nExact divisibility means the remainder is zero, so\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nm-41&=0\\\\\nn+14&=0\\\\\nm&=41,\\qquad n=-14.\n\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
